This is an independent runtime for the Phonon 31M text-to-speech model. It is not made or
endorsed by Gradium.

The model, its tokenizer and its voice catalog are by Gradium (https://gradium.ai), under the
Apache License 2.0: https://huggingface.co/gradium/phonon-31m-en and
https://huggingface.co/gradium/phonon-voices. This repository does not include them. The code
downloads the tokenizer and voices from Hugging Face at pinned revisions, and the weights
converted by scripts/build-weights.ts from https://huggingface.co/blixt/phonon-31m-en-webgpu.

Phonon builds on Pocket TTS and the Mimi codec by Kyutai (https://kyutai.org).

The benchmark compares this runtime with phonon-tts by Gradium (Apache-2.0 or MIT) and
kokoro-js by Joshua Lochner, running Kokoro 82M by hexgrad (Apache-2.0). They are development
dependencies only.

---
This house serves, unmodified, from /phonon-assets/<repo>/<revision>/<path>:
- blixt/phonon-31m-en-webgpu@f4635a6d phonon-31m-en.int8.bin (Gradium's phonon-31m-en,
  converted by blixt), Apache-2.0;
- gradium/phonon-31m-en@92741c5b tokenizer.5.0.0.json, Apache-2.0;
- gradium/phonon-voices@0ee17205 voices.jsonl and the English voices, Apache-2.0.
Each file is pinned by sha256 in config/phonon_assets.json. The runtime (phonon-webgpu,
github:blixt/phonon@36e7e5ef, Apache-2.0) is bundled with one change: its file URLs point at
/phonon-assets on this site instead of huggingface.co (patches/phonon-webgpu@*.patch).
Phonon's 40M models (CC BY-NC 4.0) are not served or used.
